{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits","id":620514,"title":"\u200b[Dark Eras] Needed Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-08T14:27:03-07:00","id":620514,"title":"\u200b[Dark Eras] Needed Merits","content":"I came to conclusion <b>Dark Eras</b> book need a few more Merits for historical chronicles. Now that the book will have at least something like 800+ pages, I think that one page for the new Merits is totally in order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Developers are more than oblige to steal those ideas to <b>Dark Eras</b> corebook.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Merits</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Literate (\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prequsition: </b>Intelligence 2+<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Before public education system ( for example, from 1833 in England ) literacy was part of only small percent of population. Even educated people not always were able to read. This Merit marks character as able to read and write in all Languages she knows and her homeland tongue . Characters with Multilingual Merit may read or write in those languages, but need to do Intelligence+Academics rolls for this.<br /> <b>Note:</b> If Storyteller allows this Merit, he should ban <i>Illiterate</i> Persistence Condition in the same Dark Era.<br /> <br /> <b>Noble (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Effect:</b> Before modern notion of \u201cevery human is born equal\u201d from the end of XIX century, almost each society had at least common man and ruling class. The second, called usually \u201cnobility\u201d, were connected with many benefits, obvious and not. This Merit represent those for character to have - as legal standing changed by centuries details and duties of nobles varied across societies the exact privilege are not listed. Most common are different legal standing in case of court and being judged, laws permitting to treat lesser classes with superiority or that permitting much more freedom in their activates.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Persistence Conditions / Flaws</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Illiterate (Persistent)</b><br /> After introducing public education system ( for example, from 1833 in England ) literacy become standard for the people. Those not able to read or write have harder time to lead their life in society based more and more on ability for citizens to read documents and making their own decisions.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>The character learn to read.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> The characters illiteracy is making problem for her life.<br /> <b>Note:</b> If Storyteller allows this Condition, he should ban <i>Literate</i> Merit in the same Dark Era.<br /> <br /> <b>Outsider (Persistent)</b><br /> This character looks and acts counter to the main society. Depending on location or history era, this character can be from untouchable caste Dalit in India or Burakumin in Japan, gay, Jew, Muslim, hippie, punk, goth or any radical counterculture of the time. Character have -1 to -3 penalty on social rolls with others depending on target conservative worldview. Mainstream target would have -1 and ultraconservative would have -3 penalty. Character also add one more Door for each penalty point to the target\u2019s pool in Social Manuvering.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Niche lifestyle. Ethnicity. Religion. Sexual orientation.<br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character integrates with mainstream. She changes her act and look to be with norm or even is lifted to proper society of location and era.<br /> <b>Beat: </b>Whenever characters status leads to conflict with authorities or community.<br /> <br /> <b>Slave (Persistent)</b><br /> Legally, character is property of other person. By the law, the cannot be disobedient to his &quot;master&quot; and his owner can make what he please with his life. Realistically, most persons fed and cared about their slaves, as they were investment, even treated as part of their families in some cases. But still, life of your character is in hands of other character.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Character is officially freed by his owner.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> The characters is disobeying his masters orders. Character's master makes him do things he does not want to ( probably leading to Breaking Point in character )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T14:46:50-07:00","id":620557,"title":"","content":"Some good work there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:24:50-07:00","id":620634,"title":"","content":"I had one more Persistent Condition:<br /> <br /> <b>Slave (Persistent)</b><br /> Legally, character is property of other person. By the law, the cannot be disobedient to his &quot;master&quot; and his owner can make what he please with his life. Realistically, most persons fed and cared about their slaves, as they were investment, even treated as part of their families in some cases. But still, life of your character is in hands of other character.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Character is officially freed by his owner.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> The characters is disobeying his masters orders. Character's master makes him do things he does not want to ( probably leading to Breaking Point in character )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-08-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:21:10-07:00","id":620739,"title":"","content":"Being literate would be better served as a part of being trained in Academics.<br /> <br /> Nobility is better served by Status.<br /> <br /> Slavery works very differently from society to society. Only recently we had societies where slaves really had no rights, that was almost unknown in the old world. That said, I'm not sure this is good as a Condition, but the rule seems good enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:37:56-07:00","id":620752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620739#post620739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being literate would be better served as a part of being trained in Academics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not agree - having Academics and being literate are not the same things. In <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday_school\" target=\"_blank\">Sunday schools English programs</a> of XVII to XVIII - and the same in whole Europe - workers were taught basic facts about history, art and religion ( best reflected by the 1st dot of Academics ) but still were mostly illiterate after program. In Middle Ages it was not weird that Noble man were illiterate and needed their personal scribes - even if they were aware of most basics of Academics Skill.<br /> <br /> That's why, I think, literacy should not be directly tied to Academics Skill - they can work separately. And yes, being Literate in old times <b>was</b> a privilege. ( And that why it should be Merit ). Sanctity of Merits make sure that even old vampires, that bought that Merit in Middle Ages can refund if if they &quot;catch up&quot; with modern society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620739#post620739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobility is better served by Status.</div> </div> </div> </div>WHAT <i>Status</i>? In Storytelling System ( nWoD rules engine ) you always have organisation the <i>Status</i> is based on - your company, church, police, etc. In the ways of Nobility it would be <i>Status (Society)</i>, I think it's too broad here because Nobility is recognized even outside of their homeland - but not in the way of strict hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Your Duke, Marquise or just Sir are all recognized even outside of their country - I think higher levels of Nobility can work with mine and Fame Merit enough good. Add Resources to mix and you got your Barons, Counts and Marquises and any title you need to. Lines of Noble Ranks are less hard than military or church seeing as most of them are only titles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-09-2015, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T19:44:09-07:00","id":620844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620752#post620752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> WHAT <i>Status</i>? In Storytelling System ( nWoD rules engine ) you always have organisation the <i>Status</i> is based on - your company, church, police, etc. In the ways of Nobility it would be <i>Status (Society)</i>, I think it's too broad here because Nobility is recognized even outside of their homeland - but not in the way of strict hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Your Duke, Marquise or just Sir are all recognized even outside of their country - I think higher levels of Nobility can work with mine and Fame Merit enough good. Add Resources to mix and you got your Barons, Counts and Marquises and any title you need to. Lines of Noble Ranks are less hard than military or church seeing as most of them are only titles.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Vampire: The Requiem 2E</b> has Kindred Status (City). Which seemed really broad to me. I expect that Nobility would have something similar. Ultimately it can be used in same way: people obey you, and you can leverage your Status to block other characters' social merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T19:52:21-07:00","id":620846,"title":"","content":"so do all vampires get the noble merit for free, as I doubt requiem for regina will be about vampire peasents :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T20:14:01-07:00","id":620850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620846#post620846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so do all vampires get the noble merit for free, as I doubt requiem for regina will be about vampire peasents :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not the Dark Ages, there are thriving urban-worker and bourgeois classes in Elizabethan England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:06:53-07:00","id":620911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree - having Academics and being literate are not the same things. In <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday_school\" target=\"_blank\">Sunday schools English programs</a> of XVII to XVIII - and the same in whole Europe - workers were that basic facts about history, art and religion ( best reflected by the 1st dot of Academics ) but still were mostly illiterate after program. In Middle Ages it was not weird that Noble man were illiterate and needed their personal scribes - even if they were aware of most basics of Academics Skill.<br /> <br /> That's why, I think, literacy should not be directly tied to Academics Skill - they can work separately. And yes, being Literate in old times <b>was</b> a privilege. ( And that why it should be Merit ). Sanctity of Merits make sure that even old vampires, that bought that Merit in Middle Ages can refund if if they &quot;catch up&quot; with modern society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of that, just think it shouldn't be reinforced mechanically through a Merit. Maybe an Academics roll (since some of the people with enough education could read at least a little), and/or be tied to second or third level of Academics. By the way, nobles who couldn't read usually weren't &quot;trained&quot; in Academics.<br /> <br /> But this could work also with other Merits. In Middle Ages access to that level or higher of education was controlled by the Church, so I think Merits associated with the Church, or able to give access to a lay tutor supported by the Church, could be enough to guarantee access to literacy. A lone Merit just for that could be reserved for someone who learned without ties to the Church.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">WHAT <i>Status</i>? In Storytelling System ( nWoD rules engine ) you always have organisation the <i>Status</i> is based on - your company, church, police, etc. In the ways of Nobility it would be <i>Status (Society)</i>, I think it's too broad here because Nobility is recognized even outside of their homeland - but not in the way of strict hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Your Duke, Marquise or just Sir are all recognized even outside of their country - I think higher levels of Nobility can work with mine and Fame Merit enough good. Add Resources to mix and you got your Barons, Counts and Marquises and any title you need to. Lines of Noble Ranks are less hard than military or church seeing as most of them are only titles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you simply got it wrong. Heraldry is a minor thing now, but until the revolutions from the XIX century it was far more relevant, and rigid. To begin with, a noble title is directly equivalent to a military rank. It isn't now, but it WAS them. It also played a key role in medieval law, determining your rights and duties. Finally, it was key also to determine your relation with lands. Land was a major resource back them, but wasn't really your property. All land belonged to the King, and nobles had access and right over it as much as they had administrative and defensive obligations. And title was key to determine these roles.<br /> <br /> A noble doesn't had to be rich. In fact, some where poor. Even Dukes and Kings could face hardships enough to become poor. But they where still Dukes and Kings, with all the social standing and rights entitled to them. Maybe Status (Heraldry) would make for it. What these titles do is to determine your position in the hierarchy of the medieval state. If you think it too broad, make every dot of Status (Heraldry) cost double. Resources and Fame are common among nobles, but not necessary, and some commoners also could achieve both, as was the case of some villeins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:52:15-07:00","id":620930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620844#post620844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Vampire: The Requiem 2E</b> has Kindred Status (City). Which seemed really broad to me. I expect that Nobility would have something similar. Ultimately it can be used in same way: people obey you, and you can leverage your Status to block other characters' social merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Status, even in City, is <i>very</i> different than being the Noble - graphically speaking, Nobles should have &quot;Status(World)&quot; and it still be distinct in every country and in different times. I think that 3 dots Merit ( maybe even 2 dot ) like True Friend is solving this kind of problems - in past being Noble was living in the world on it self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620846#post620846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so do all vampires get the noble merit for free, as I doubt requiem for regina will be about vampire peasents :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Basiclly what GlamourWeaver says:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620850#post620850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It's not the Dark Ages, there are thriving urban-worker and bourgeois classes in Elizabethan England.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, giving Merits for free is totally okey in nWoD. Mage 2ED Template gives you High Speech, Rotes ( that are practically Merits ) and Rote Specialization in Orders, even if those are Merits in game just for free.<br /> <br /> If your ST wants to run an only Court drama, he should give you Noble Merit for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620911#post620911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm aware of that, just think it shouldn't be reinforced mechanically through a Merit. Maybe an Academics roll (since some of the people with enough education could read at least a little), and/or be tied to second or third level of Academics. By the way, nobles who couldn't read usually weren't &quot;trained&quot; in Academics.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Usually&quot; is crutial word - the norm was true, you learned Academics and also learn to read. BUT NOT ALWAYS. And for those &quot;Not Always&quot; is typical used Merits. Also, being Literate is slight boost to your social status in society at large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620911#post620911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this could work also with other Merits. In Middle Ages access to that level or higher of education was controlled by the Church, so I think Merits associated with the Church, or able to give access to a lay tutor supported by the Church, could be enough to guarantee access to literacy. A lone Merit just for that could be reserved for someone who learned without ties to the Church.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now this is a slight hypocrisy of you - you write that Literacy should not be a Merit, but now you make it part of other Merit? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I agree that if we make Literacy as 1 dot Merit, that Status in Church of Middle Ages - that should really work with perks like Mystery Cult Initiation - should give you Literacy Merit on first dot for free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=620911#post620911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now you simply got it wrong. Heraldry is a minor thing now, but until the revolutions from the XIX century it was far more relevant, and rigid. To begin with, a noble title is directly equivalent to a military rank. It isn't now, but it WAS them. It also played a key role in medieval law, determining your rights and duties. Finally, it was key also to determine your relation with lands. Land was a major resource back them, but wasn't really your property. All land belonged to the King, and nobles had access and right over it as much as they had administrative and defensive obligations. And title was key to determine these roles.<br /> <br /> A noble doesn't had to be rich. In fact, some where poor. Even Dukes and Kings could face hardships enough to become poor. But they where still Dukes and Kings, with all the social standing and rights entitled to them. Maybe Status (Heraldry) would make for it. What these titles do is to determine your position in the hierarchy of the medieval state. If you think it too broad, make every dot of Status (Heraldry) cost double. Resources and Fame are common among nobles, but not necessary, and some commoners also could achieve both, as was the case of some villeins.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I can agree I made too big assumptions here. But still, from what you write, Nobility should be like Status (World) in past Eras - you are higher on social ladder <b>from every other</b>, beside the other nobles. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-09-2015, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T12:27:52-08:00","id":760844,"title":"","content":"The more I think about Middle Ages eras and watch shows like <b><i>Vikings</i></b> or <i><b>Last Kingdom</b></i> - the more I come to conclusion that Christians should get for free a Merit <b>Virtuous ( Faith )</b>, because half of their decisions are only logical if you take them through the ramifications of Church dogma, really. It <i>really</i> looks like they normal, personal Virtue is competing with Faith on day to day basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T13:27:16-08:00","id":760893,"title":"","content":"1) Christians would just pick personal Breaking Points that reflect their faith. You didn't do your religious stuff because it was self-affirming, you did it because that's what was expected of you and that's what you had been taught was right. Self-esteem and self-affirmation weren't really things that were encouraged back then.<br /> <br /> 2) Status <i>would</i> cover nobility - Status covers your ability to throw your weight around in a particular place (your home country). The reason you get more of an ear when you're off in foreign places is <i>not</i> because you can throw your divine right to nobility around, it's because you have <i>stuff</i> back home that you can give them (also, you might be their cousin.) Think of it like having Status in, say, the government - people are going to be nice to you if you're a governor, even if you don't actually have any authority over them.<br /> <br /> 3) You wouldn't get one dot of Academics from Sunday school - you might get Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics); assuming, of course, that 'Sunday school' is a thing in your country, which it very well could not be. Similarly, the education a noble receives is probably closer to a dot of Expression, Politics, and Persuasion, with Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics) and maybe a couple copies of Multilingual being tossed in there. So having a single dot of Academics probably would cover literacy as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:01:21-08:00","id":761205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=760893#post760893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Christians would just pick personal Breaking Points that reflect their faith. You didn't do your religious stuff because it was self-affirming, you did it because that's what was expected of you and that's what you had been taught was right. Self-esteem and self-affirmation weren't really things that were encouraged back then.</div> </div> </div> </div>I talk here about characters like <a href=\"http://the-last-kingdom.wikia.com/wiki/Alfred\" target=\"_blank\">Alfred the Great</a> - on one hand, he is Prudent, reasonable strategist ( I really think he should have <i>Prudence</i> as Virtue ). On the other hand, he spands half time on prayer, he tries to forgive his enemies and be &quot;good Christian&quot;. It's much more than simply &quot;You will not break Gods Commandments&quot; as Breaking Point - half of his life is dedicated to Church and <i>Faith</i>.<br /> <br /> And it's all over the Christian world - half of <i><b>Last Kingdom</b></i> cast is really dedicated to <i>Faith</i>, even if they are also dedicated to other Virtues.<br /> <br /> On the side, Alfred probably would have also <b>Vice-Ridden</b> Merit, as he is both <i>Prideful</i> and <i>Lustful </i>- but it's more sidenote here.<br /> <br /> Point is - most Christian have two Virtues, fighting over they behavior - one of them is Faith, other is their normal, personal Virtue. And omiting Breaking Points of Christianity is not enough to portray them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T22:12:13-08:00","id":761250,"title":"","content":"I think you may be overthinking this. Christianity is not so special as to merit that being a norm of adherents to the religion, and sources on these figures, having been mostly written by members of religious institutions in a culture of hyperbole (That is, medieval writing) really lends itself to exaggerating the virtues of its heroes. Especially their Christian virtues.<br /> <br /> I figure how much truth that has is a subject for individual games, but for what it's worth, I'd err on the side of skepticism if you're trying to approach this with a critical eye towards history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T02:15:06-08:00","id":761325,"title":"","content":"To me Status suggest something you can change. The reality is that depending on the era and society there was very little you could change about the station of your life. If you run a game in for example feudal Europe or medieval Japan, you either are a noble or not. I think in such a time it is better done through a Nobility merit gained at character generation. Of course, if you are wealthy and powerful enough you can always fake your station, but don't let the others learn about it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mind you, that is the biggest issue with all of these is that if you write a book covering a large period of time and geography you are bound to run into the huge differences between what it meant to be a slave among the Romans, feudal Europe or 19th century Caribbean, let alone the differences between a Roman noble (didn't mean much), feudal noble or noble in the Victorian age. You need a new text for each of those <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:09:52-08:00","id":761412,"title":"","content":"May be an option could be Status (nobility), with each doy representing a rank: Knight, baron, count, duke... Whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:00:05-07:00","id":1067458,"title":"","content":"Reading Black Death Dark Era in Companion - <i>Soulless and Dead</i> - I remembered this topic and want to return to it and as Era does not solve problems with Nobility higher status by the rules. I still aiming more for making Nobility as seperate Merit, maybe it's own Status...<br /> <br /> Also, reading about Social Classes of 14th century Europe, I see that new Persistent Condition / Flaw will be totally in order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dar Eras Companion, p. 89</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, this potential for mobility leads to bitter competition amongst the lower (but not the very lowest) echelons of society that led to strife. Persecution of gays, Jews, Muslims, and heretics increases throughout the century. (...) It\u2019s a bad time to be an outsider.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Outsider (Persistent)</b><br /> This character looks and acts counter to the main society. Depending on location or history era, this character can be from untouchable caste Dalit in India or Burakumin in Japan, gay, Jew, Muslim, hippie, punk, goth or any radical counterculture of the time. Character have -1 to -3 penalty on social rolls with others depending on target conservative worldview. Mainstream target would have -1 and ultraconservative would have -3 penalty. Character also add one more Door for each penalty point to the target\u2019s pool in Social Manuvering.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> Niche lifestyle. Ethnicity. Religion. Sexual orientation.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution: </b>Character integrates with mainstream. She changes her act and look to be with norm or even is lifted to proper society of location and era.<br /> <br /> <b>Beat: </b>Whenever characters status leads to conflict with authorities or community.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:27:45-07:00","id":1067493,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't use Literate as a Merit and Illiterate as a Flaw at the same time. Pick one for your baseline for player characters. If the baseline is literacy, than illiteracy is a flaw. If the baseline is illiteracy, than literacy is a Merit.<br /> <br /> If you want to get really fiddly with it though, you could have players pick one and it's neither a Merit or flaw, but illiteracy comes with bonuses to oral recollection that don't apply if you're literate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-24-2017, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:37:07-07:00","id":1067496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067493#post1067493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't use Literate as a Merit and Illiterate as a Flaw at the same table. Pick one for your baseline for player characters. If the baseline is literacy, than illiteracy is a flaw. If the baseline is illiteracy, than literacy is a Merit..</div> </div> </div> </div>It's default assumption. More, <b>Dark Eras</b> corebook states almost exactly this in introduction. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But I will reword both mechanics to be much clearer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T06:58:12-07:00","id":1067550,"title":"","content":"Why not just use 'Status: Nobility'?<br /> Nobility is something you are given, since historically even those of noble blood had to earn their title. Nobility is something that can be taken from you, as shown when noble families like my ancestors are stripped of their lands and power. Nobility is something that can 'level up' through deeds, tithings, and political connections.<br /> Lastly, nobility is something universally recognized but not universally respected; because of the isolationist cultures and tribes of the time, it was possible to come to lands where your heraldry was not recognized even within 'your' own kingdom. Seems just like Status to me, it just carries a few extra perks (freeish 'Staff') and a few drawbacks (Fealty).<br /> <br /> I'd suggest this be a creation-only merit, because climbing the rungs of nobility is much easier than getting credit for noble actions as a commonfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","user":"Necrophear","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11102-necrophear","name":"Necrophear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11102_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:02:04-07:00","id":1067627,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure why we need a Noble merit when you could just as easily keep that abstracted in roleplay or else represent it with high Resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:05:20-07:00","id":1067629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067627#post1067627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure why we need a Noble merit when you could just as easily keep that abstracted in roleplay or else represent it with high Resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from my perspective. Nobles have huge advantage in previous Eras. It's a reason you want to be a knighte or Jarl. In the eyes of the law, you are above any one else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:26:00-07:00","id":1067641,"title":"","content":"I see both sides pretty clearly. In every <i>Requiem for Rome </i>game (and my long running Roman Vigil game) I've run, I've always considered one dot of Academics to be the equivalent of literacy, and I have flat out told my players without Academics, &quot;you can't read it.&quot; So I'd probably just keep doing that. That being said, &quot;Literate&quot; is a one-point merit in <i>V20 Dark Ages</i>, which I know is not CofD, but it's definitely a good point of comparison. I think a one-dot merit for Literacy in some Dark Eras isn't too much of a stretch if an ST would like to use that in order to free up Academics to also represent knowledge known from being read to or preached at.<br /> <br /> I <i>love </i>some of these conditions, though, such as &quot;slave&quot; and &quot;outsider.&quot; I find it hard to believe that &quot;outsider&quot; might ever have a resolution, since integration within one's lifetime is all but impossible. An Irish vampire in New York in the 1910s, however, might lose the outsider status sometime around the 60s, though, if he survives that long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:39:04-07:00","id":1067676,"title":"","content":"My inclination for pre-movable-type societies is use illiterate as the default, make literacy a 1 point merit, and give it for free if they buy academics over 1 dot (unless it's a society without writing whose lore is entirely oral). Post-movable-type, literacy is the default, illiteracy is a flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-24-2017, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:42:31-07:00","id":1067683,"title":"","content":"Maybe this is showing my mechanical preferences too strongly, but I'm not sure literacy or social class need mechanics. Why not just have that be RP?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:17:23-07:00","id":1067703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067683#post1067683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this is showing my mechanical preferences too strongly, but I'm not sure literacy or social class need mechanics. Why not just have that be RP?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it makes sense for Illiteracy to be a Condition the same way physical disability is - essentially a nice gesture for the players who want to roleplay a disadvantage. Or, if illiteracy is the assumed default in your setting, then attaching a small cost to the roleplaying advantage makes sense. But yeah, I don't really see a need for special mechanics for things like social class. Especially because we have a Status Merit already and that's exactly what social class is. Economic class, we have Resources for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:23:34-07:00","id":1067704,"title":"","content":"Okay, let's assume we go with Noble social class as Status - how would it look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:31:08-07:00","id":1067710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067704#post1067704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let's assume we go with Noble social class as Status - how would it look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... Like any other Status? If you want to be a powerful noble, you take Status (Nobility). You get a bonus equal to your dots in the Merit on Social rolls with people who recognize your claim to nobility, and can use your Status dots to acquire Equipment and Services, and to cut off other characters' access to their Social Merits. No need to reinvent the wheel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:19:22-07:00","id":1067760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067710#post1067710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... Like any other Status?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean about Status levels of Nobility - like were the Count, Baron, etc. would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:19:22-07:00","id":1067785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067760#post1067760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean about Status levels of Nobility - like were the Count, Baron, etc. would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. I wouldn't make it that rigid. Much as a vampire Prince can have City Status 1 if he wields little actual power, a mortal lord could have Nobility Status 1 if he is not respected or feared by his serfs. More flexibility is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T22:31:24-07:00","id":1067924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067785#post1067785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I see. I wouldn't make it that rigid. Much as a vampire Prince can have City Status 1 if he wields little actual power, a mortal lord could have Nobility Status 1 if he is not respected or feared by his serfs. More flexibility is better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is, and it is not. For example, in<b> Mage</b>, most of positions have certin Order Status level requirements. ( They can be sometimes missed from the story preservative, but then it's assumed character has lacking background and NPCs are waiting to show his weakness on position. ) I suspect the same would be with Nobility ( Status ), so that's why I asking on examples.<br /> <br /> Like I prepare Viking Werewolf game - How could I represent Jarls and Housekarls in the setting with Status ( Nobility )?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2017, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:07:35-07:00","id":1067928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1067924#post1067924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it is, and it is not. For example, in<b> Mage</b>, most of positions have certin Order Status level requirements. ( They can be sometimes missed from the story preservative, but then it's assumed character has lacking background and NPCs are waiting to show his weakness on position. ) I suspect the same would be with Nobility ( Status ), so that's why I asking on examples.<br /> <br /> Like I prepare Viking Werewolf game - How could I represent Jarls and Housekarls in the setting with Status ( Nobility )?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's going to depend on the power of the Jarl. Speaking very broadly, I might say a Thrall cannot have Nobility Status, being an unfree person. A Karl is not noble, but might have Nobility Status 1 or 2 if they are favored by the local Jarl - for example, if they serve in his Longhouse (a Housekarl), or if they are empowered to speak in support of him at the Thing. A Jarl may have Nobility Status anywhere from 1 to 5, depending on how much power he has and how far his influence spreads, but most will fall somewhere in the 2-3 range. A king won't usually have Nobility Status below 3 unless he is very unpopular with the other nobles, and will usually have 4 or 5 if he has proven himself to be a good leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-25-2017, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:17:38-07:00","id":1067968,"title":"","content":"I want to point out that 2E has moved away from the Status Prerequisites for positions and further initiation. Some of the merits do still have more than one Status dot as a prereq, but most seem to have a single Status dot as prereq. When you're a member. For example Egregore, which is the continued initiation in the deeper mysteries in the Mysterium, has a total prereq of one Status dot.<br /> <br /> Your viking game is set in Sweden before year 1000, yes? In that case I want to point out that nobility didn't quite exist. At least not in the way we think about nobility. The only class barrier were between thralls and free people. Anyone who were free had the potential to become a jarl.<br /> Only later did huskarls become nobility when Sweden (and the rest of Scandinavia) adopted mainland nobility customs. Depending on exactly when you set your game, Wyrd, huskarls could be either just hired manservants or hired elite infantery or anything inbetween. Either way their position was actually just a job, even if a very prestigious job towards the end of the millennium. <br /> So, while it probably wasn't easy to climb the socioeconomical ladder, there were no hard barrier between the common free people and the proto-/semi-nobility of jarls and late huskarls. That's why I think it's better to still use Status. If you want jarls to have any mechanical benefits, just create a separate Jarl Merit to represent that, just like positions in different organizations can have individual Merits.<br /> <br /> (Huskarl is literally house man, which basically meant manservant. Shorten it to karl and you just get the word for man.)<br /> <br /> Edit: I did not talk about Swedish kings before the second millennium, but that's because there's very little information about them. It's almost certain we had some, but we can't verify any individuals.<br /> <br /> I also want to put a disclaimer here saying that I'm not an expert on the subject and parts of what I've written may not be 100% accurate despite me trying to verify my information while writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-25-2017, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:54:45-07:00","id":1068009,"title":"","content":"The museum I work at recently opened a temporary exhibit about Vikings, so while I am not an expert either, I have been steeped in research about them and talking to experts for the past few months. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>, what you said is fairly consistent with what I've been learning. I would add, however, that while theoretically any man could become a Jarl, in practice there was probably very little upward mobility for free men except by marrying into more powerful families. And there was likely at least some perception that Jarls came from different lineage than Karls, who came from different lineage than Thralls, which you can see in the eddic poem, Rigsmal, which explains the origin of the Viking social classes by telling that Rig/Heimdall fathered three children named Thrall, Karl, and Jarl each from a different human couple, and goes on to describe their features and those of their descendants.<br /> <br /> And yeah, housekarl isn't a social class at this time, it's a job people of the social class Karl might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-25-2017, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T18:23:21-07:00","id":1544368,"title":"","content":"Topic Necromancy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If in Mage, at the start of Orders in 3rd century BCE, mages are not always Literate - should they get this Merit for free, cause their proto-Orders give them?<br /> <br /> Mage 2ED Template gives you High Speech, Rotes ( that are practically Merits ) and Rote Specialization in Orders, even if those are Merits in game, just for free.\ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T13:23:03-07:00","id":1544586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/620514-\u200b-dark-eras-needed-merits?p=1544368#post1544368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Topic Necromancy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If in Mage, at the start of Orders in 3rd century BCE, mages are not always Literate - should they get this Merit for free, cause their proto-Orders give them?<br /> <br /> Mage 2ED Template gives you High Speech, Rotes ( that are practically Merits ) and Rote Specialization in Orders, even if those are Merits in game, just for free.\ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't think mages generally have that kind of time to waste. Like, the benefits of the modern Orders are pretty quick to teach and can be done 'on the job' more or less, whilst literacy takes years of dedicated hard work. (Though, I suppose you could handwave that with Mind magic; like, if you have a literacy spell cast on you enough times, it eventually just sticks.)<br /> <br /> Some Orders, in some places, probably do teach literacy as a matter of course. Like, a Roman proto-Sacristan probably does. A Roman Phulakes though? Like, sure it'd be handy, but they can probably fulfil most of their duties without it.<br /> <br /> Additionally, though we tend to lump reading and writing together as one skill, that's not necessarily true. I gather that a lot of famous Roman authors actually dictated their words to a scribe. Makes me wonder if there was once a vast cadre of sleepwalker scribes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}